("note", "FORMULA", "**Slant height of a cone: l = &radic;(r<sup>2</sup> + h<sup>2</sup>).**  Cone: radius 7, height 24, so l = 25, CSA = (22/7)(7)(25) = **550**, TSA = 550 + 154 = **704**, volume = (1/3)(22/7)(49)(24) = **1232**. Cylinder (7, 10): volume = 1540, TSA = 2(22/7)(7)(17) = **748**."),
("h2", "12.2 Combination of Solids"),
("note", "IMPORTANT", "When two solids are joined, the **surfaces that meet become hidden**, so the **total surface area of the combination is the sum of the visible curved (or flat) areas**, **not** the sum of the TSAs. **Volume** of the combination is simply the **sum of the volumes**."),
("table", ["Combination", "Visible surface area", "Volume"], [["Cone on a hemisphere (toy, top)", "CSA of cone + CSA of hemisphere", "Cone + hemisphere"], ["Cylinder with hemispherical ends (capsule)", "CSA of cylinder + 2 hemispherical CSAs", "Cylinder + sphere of same radius"], ["Cylinder with a cone on top (tent, rocket)", "CSA cylinder + CSA cone + base if closed below", "Cylinder + cone"], ["Cylinder with a hemispherical hollow at one end", "CSA of cylinder + CSA of hemisphere + remaining ring/base area", "Cylinder &minus; hemisphere"], ["Cube with a hemispherical depression", "TSA of cube &minus; &pi;r<sup>2</sup> + 2&pi;r<sup>2</sup>", "Cube &minus; hemisphere"]]),
("p", "**Example (toy).** A cone of radius 7 cm and height 24 cm stands on a hemisphere of radius 7 cm. Surface area = cone CSA 550 + hemisphere CSA 2(22/7)(49) = 308, total **858 cm<sup>2</sup>**. Volume = 1232 + (2/3)(22/7)(343) = 1232 + 718.67 = **1950.67 cm<sup>3</sup>**."),
("p", "**Example (capsule).** A capsule has a cylinder of length 5 mm and radius 2 mm with hemispherical ends. Surface area = 2&pi;rh + 2(2&pi;r<sup>2</sup>) = 2&pi;(2)(5) + 4&pi;(4) = 20&pi; + 16&pi; = 36&pi; = **113.1 mm<sup>2</sup>**. Volume = &pi;(4)(5) + (4/3)&pi;(8) = 20&pi; + 32&pi;/3 = **96.3 mm<sup>3</sup>**."),
("p", "**Example (wooden cylinder with a hemispherical scoop at each end).** TSA = CSA of cylinder + 2 x CSA of hemisphere, as the flat circular faces are removed and replaced by curved faces."),
("h2", "12.3 Conversion of a Solid into Another"),
("note", "FORMULA", "When a solid is melted and recast, **volume remains the same**: volume of the original = volume of the new solid(s). If n identical pieces are made, **n x (volume of one) = volume of the original**."),
